description:
In repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/feature-compose.ts, attach the refusal trace's execution identifier to the report body so a refused compose can be graded instead of falling back to a synthetic identifier that the grader skips.

Measured on the live substrate: when goal-host receives a report carrying a real execution identifier it grades the row successfully, logging reach-patch ok with reached false and rows one. When the report has no identifier it falls back to a synthesised feature_compose identifier, and that prefix is on the grader's synthetic skip list, so the verdict is never delivered at all and the arm's posterior cannot move. The refusal path currently reads the identifier the trace store returns, logs it, and discards it, which is precisely the discarded-response defect this file already fixed on its main path.

Perform exactly one replacement. Find the sole occurrence of this line:
          if (typeof refusalId === "string" && refusalId.length > 0) {

Replace it with these lines:
          if (typeof refusalId === "string" && refusalId.length > 0) {
            if (outcome && typeof outcome === "object" && outcome.body && typeof outcome.body === "object") {
              (outcome.body as Record<string, unknown>)["execution_id"] = refusalId;
            }

This assigns the captured identifier onto the report body that is about to be returned, so the caller receives the real row address. The existing log line immediately below is unchanged and still runs, the enclosing guards and the swallowing catch are untouched, and the return of outcome at the end of the block is unchanged. The main non-refusal path already sets an execution_id field on its report body in the same way, so this makes the refusal path consistent with it.

One replacement, one file. Change nothing else.

